The fifth film in the DC Extended Universe (DCEU) is "Justice League," which was released in 2017. It is a superhero film based on the DC Comics team of the same name and is directed by Zack Snyder, with a screenplay written by Chris Terrio and Joss Whedon. The film features an ensemble cast including Ben Affleck as Batman, Henry Cavill as Superman, Gal Gadot as Wonder Woman, Ezra Miller as The Flash, Jason Momoa as Aquaman, and Ray Fisher as Cyborg. Supporting roles are played by Amy Adams, Jeremy Irons, Diane Lane, Connie Nielsen, and J. K. Simmons. 

The film was initially set to be released in 2016 but was delayed due to production issues and mixed critical reception. Following its release, there were some reshuffling of film production staff at Warner Bros. due to the film's performance. The storyline of "Justice League" involves the team uniting to face the threat posed by the alien villain Steppenwolf.
